      "id": "rh898ew",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Himalayan Mountain System"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Himalayas are young fold mountains extending approximately 2,400 km from the Indus to the Brahmaputra.",
        "The Trans-Himalayan region consists of the Karakoram, Ladakh, Zaskar, and Kailash ranges.",
        "Anamudi is the highest peak in South India and the Peninsular Plateau, located in the Western Ghats.",
        "The Aravalli Range is one of the oldest fold mountain systems in the world, with Guru Shikhar as its highest point.",
        "The Western Ghats form a continuous wall along the western coast, while the Eastern Ghats are discontinuous and heavily dissected by rivers."
      ],
      "id": "68khqn7"
    },
